      ],
      "name": "Reverse Grip Ezbar Curls",
      "notes": "Hold the barbell with an overhand grip (palms facing down) approximately shoulder-width apart. Ensure your back is straight, shoulders slightly pulled back, and arms fully extended.\nCurl the barbell upwards towards your chest in a controlled motion, keeping your elbows close to your body. The motion should be smooth without any swinging or momentum use.\nOnce the barbell is at chest level, pause briefly to maximize contraction in the biceps and forearms.\nSlowly lower the barbell back to the starting position with a controlled movement, fully extending your arms."
    },
